To determine the validity of the statement "More than half of the world's population uses the internet" while taking into account geographical location, socioeconomic status, age, and device usage, we need to analyze data from various sources. We can use data from the World Bank, International Telecommunication Union (ITU), and other reputable sources.
MATLAB can be used to analyze the data and provide a more accurate categorization. Here is an example MATLAB code that can perform this analysis:
```matlab
% Load data from World Bank and ITU
wbData = readtable('WorldBankData.xlsx');
ituData = readtable('ITUData.xlsx');
% Merge data based on country code
mergedData = outerjoin(wbData,ituData,'MergeKeys',true);
% Clean the data by removing NaN values
cleanData = mergedData(~any(ismissing(mergedData),2),:);
% Calculate the percentage of internet users by country
cleanData.InternetUsersPercentage = cleanData.InternetUsers/cleanData.Population*100;
% Group the data by geographical location, socioeconomic status, age, and device usage
geographicalLocation = {'North America','Europe','Asia','Africa','South America'};
socioeconomicStatus = {'High income','Upper middle income','Lower middle income','Low income'};
age = {'15-24','25-34','35-44','45-54','55-64','65+'};
deviceUsage = {'Mobile','Fixed broadband','Total'};
for i = 1:length(geographicalLocation)
    for j = 1:length(socioeconomicStatus)
        for k = 1:length(age)
            for l = 1:length(deviceUsage)
                groupData = cleanData(cleanData.Region==geographicalLocation{i} & ...
                                      strcmp(cleanData.IncomeGroup,socioeconomicStatus{j}) & ...
                                      strcmp(cleanData.AgeGroup,age{k}) & ...
                                      strcmp(cleanData.DeviceType,deviceUsage{l}),:);
                if ~isempty(groupData)
                    percentage = mean(groupData.InternetUsersPercentage);
                    fprintf('Geographical Location: %s, Socioeconomic Status: %s, Age: %s, Device Usage: %s, Percentage of Internet Users: %.2f%%\n', ...
                            geographicalLocation{i}, socioeconomicStatus{j}, age{k}, deviceUsage{l}, percentage);
                end
            end
        end
    end
end
